# A listing of all a directory holds lists the directory: `iterdir()` lists what `glob("*")` lists, the fiber over a
# predicate that always holds, and each element is one of the folders below it, `*`. `KINDS[..]` with a key the
# environment says is one of the values the mapping holds: two directories. A sort key's parameter is one of the paths
# it orders: `p.stat()` reads at the place `m.glob("*.xml")` holds, as `max(..)`'s file, read after it, is.

route listed.run
line entry > run call
line File(assets/regelingen/) > run own                  # (..).iterdir() lists the directory
line File(assets/ontwerp_regelingen/) > run own
line File(assets/regelingen/*/*.xml) > run own           # m.glob(..), p.stat(), max(..).read_text()
line File(assets/ontwerp_regelingen/*/*.xml) > run own
line run > Screen own

side entry left
side File(assets/regelingen/) left
side File(assets/ontwerp_regelingen/) left
side File(assets/regelingen/*/*.xml) left
side File(assets/ontwerp_regelingen/*/*.xml) left
side Screen right
